<title>CHILE: Argentine quake causes no damage to Chile copper.</title>
<headline>Argentine quake causes no damage to Chile copper.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 6.4 on the Richter scale in northern Argentina caused no damage or injuries at copper mines over the border in Chile, mine officials said.</p>
<p>The quake, at 0215 GMT Thursday, had its epicenter in the Argentine province of Jujuy near the Bolivian border, Universidad de Chile's seismology department reported.</p>
<p>The quake was felt in much of northern Chile but caused no damage at all at the two nearest major mines, Codelco's Chuquicamata and Cyprus Amax Minerals' El Abra, officials at both mines told Reuters Wednesday night when the quake happened and again Thursday morning.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
